        <!--
            To add a new release:

            1. Archive and export the app (Product > Archive in Xcode)
            2. Sign the .zip with the Sparkle sign_update tool:

               ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/docketizer-.../SourcePackages/artifacts/sparkle/Sparkle/bin/sign_update docketizer-1.1.0.zip

               The tool prints the edSignature and length values to paste below.

            3. Copy this <item> block, fill in the new version details and upload
               the .zip + updated appcast.xml to your server.
        -->

        <item>
            <title>Version 1.1</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:51:34 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>2</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description
            ><![CDATA[
                <h3>What's new</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>The week overview now shows how much of your required working hours you have tracked per day. Days with all hours tracked turn green.</li>
                    <li>Days without required hours (e.g. weekends) are shown more subtle.</li>
                    <li>Switching weeks now updates the overview right away.</li>
                    <li>Available updates are now shown unobtrusively via a dot on the menu bar icon and a button in the footer.</li>
                    <li>Support for 2FA login.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
